# Charge a NON-SPECIALIST mage by character generation, then create undead with the
# wizard's Create Corporeal Undead and photograph the Group CR Totals block.
# bd inc-1n74, tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh.
#
# THE GRANT UNDER TEST COMES FROM lib/classes.irh AT GENERATION TIME. A level-1
# Necromancer is given BONUS_PHD of magnitude 1 against PHD_UNDEAD; a mage of
# any other school is not. So this script must RUN the chargen -- loading a
# frozen .sav would bake in whichever lib made that save, and the check could
# not go red on the lib mutation (see tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh).
#
# The chargen below is tools/keys/chargen-mage.keys' character (male orc mage,
# neutral, first attribute set, first two feats, three RIGHTs per skill) with
# one change: the school is Evocation. It is the comparison to
# tools/keys/necro-undead-pool-necro.keys, which is the same file with
# Necromancy, so the only difference between the two characters is the school.
#
# WHY THERE ARE SEVERAL CASTS. One wight proves the GRANT (PHD UNDEAD 2 / 1).
# The admission change in Monster::MakeCompanion's PHD_UNDEAD branch needs more:
# it must REFUSE a created undead once undead + magic + party are full. So after
# the grant reading this script raises wight after wight on the corpses the
# level leaves behind. Each cast is photographed twice: the cast screen, which
# carries the caller's own verdict ("The dead rise!" or "shifts briefly, but
# does not move", lib/abilities.irh:179/187), and the wizard Group CR Totals
# block, which carries the count that actually joined. The message window is
# only a few lines deep and a created undead angers many gods, so the window
# can scroll "The dead rise!" away; the pool reading is the reliable count.
# On the fixed code the third attempt is refused and the pool stops growing.
# The mutated run (tools/check_necro_undead_pool.sh --prove-red) sends the
# PHD_UNDEAD case back to the generic branch, which never refuses here.
#
# TARGETING. The corpses are the level's own, at fixed offsets from the player
# (the player never moves). Create Corporeal Undead's target prompt takes 'l'
# to move the location cursor, then arrow keys to the square: UP*3 LEFT is the
# elf corpse, DOWN LEFT*4 the human, DOWN*4 the dwarf, DOWN*3 LEFT the gnome,
# DOWN*2 RIGHT*3 the kobold. The ring arrows cannot be used here -- after the
# first wight they include the wights themselves, and the prompt stops on one.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Mage"
a       # Attributes
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Evocation"
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y
y       # Worship the offered god
a       # Personality archetype
a a a   # Three starting spells
x       # Dismiss the arrival room description

@until "Things in View" ESC
w y                     # Enter wizard mode and confirm.

# Infinite Mana (Table row 8) lets a level 1 mage cast a level 5 spell.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7 SPACE
ESC

# Create Corporeal Undead is not on the mage list; Learn Any Spell makes it known.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Create Corporeal Undead" ENTER

# A black orc east of the player, so the level holds a medium humanoid corpse.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Orc"
a
RIGHT*3 ENTER

# Clear the level, leaving the corpse(s) and nothing else that makes a pool move.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
SPACE*40                 # dismiss the genocide message chain

# The control reading: no undead yet. Necromancer PHD UNDEAD max 1, other mage 0.
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group-before
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 1: the elf corpse. This is a real Monster::MakeCompanion(PHD_UNDEAD)
# caller (lib/abilities.irh:177).
m
a
l
UP*3 LEFT ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:raised
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group-after
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 2: the human corpse. Kept under the fixed code.
m
a
l
DOWN LEFT*4 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast2
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group2
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 3: the dwarf corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
DOWN*4 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast3
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group3
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 4: the gnome corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
DOWN*3 LEFT ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast4
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group4
ESC
SPACE*4

# Cast 5: the kobold corpse. REFUSED under the fixed code.
m
a
l
DOWN*2 RIGHT*3 ENTER
@choose "Wight"
@dump:cast5
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*200
@dump:group5
ESC
SPACE*4

@quit
